    "First-generation migrants borrowed many English words but declined them like Greek ones. “Book” became *το μπούκο*, with a neuter ending added so it could fit Greek grammar. Elsewhere speakers translate English expressions word for word, such as *άνοιξε το φως* (“open the light”, from English “turn on” via other migrant languages) instead of standard *άναψε το φως*. Linguists such as Anastasios Tamis have studied this mixture, which is now fading as younger people learn either standard Greek or English only.",
