       en="Loanwords in standard Greek are usually **invariable neuters**: *το μπαρ, το σάντουιτς, το κομπιούτερ*. In migrant speech they are often **adapted** with a Greek ending to show gender and case: *το μπούκο, τα μπούκα*. Standard Greek has older adapted loans of the same kind: *η τσάντα* (Turkish), *η μπάλα* (Italian), *το φλιτζάνι* (Turkish).",
